 **Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
 
+### Specialty directory
+
+<a id="req-spec-001"></a>
+
+The clinic publishes its specialties as the inverse of the veterinarian directory: where that page answers "which specialties does this veterinarian hold", this one answers "which veterinarians hold this specialty". Every specialty the clinic knows is listed by its stored name, each with the veterinarians who hold it shown by full name — first name then last name, as in "Helen Leary". A veterinarian holding no specialty appears under no specialty at all: the page presents specialties with the veterinarians grouped beneath them, not the full veterinarian roster. Every specialty renders on a single page, without the paging the veterinarian directory uses. Reading and presenting the directory is all it does; managing veterinarians or specialties stays out of scope under NG-2 `[REQ-SPEC-001]`.
+
+**Done when:**
+- `[REQ-SPEC-001]` given the clinic's specialties, when the specialty directory is opened, then every specialty is listed by its stored name, each with the veterinarians who hold it shown by full name (first name then last name).
+- `[REQ-SPEC-001]` given a veterinarian who holds no specialty, when the directory is opened, then that veterinarian does not appear — the page lists specialties and the veterinarians beneath them, not every veterinarian the clinic employs.
+- `[REQ-SPEC-001]` given the clinic's specialties, when the directory is opened, then all of them render on one page, with no pagination.
+
+**Edge cases:**
+1. The specialties are presented in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one.
+2. A specialty is listed because it is stored, independently of how many veterinarians hold it.
+
+**Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
+
 ### Language
 
 <a id="req-lang-001"></a><a id="req-lang-002"></a>
